# In Flex 3 and Flex 4, I used lookup formulas in Excel and joins in Tableau to connect my tables, and I had to redo my summaries by hand 
#whenever the data changed. Power BI does this for me, I set up how the tables connect one time, and every chart updates on its own. For 
#something that gets ran every month I would use Power BI, because everyone gets the same numbers and there is less chance of a mistake. 
#A broken formula or a forgotten update can give a wrong answer without anyone noticing, and that risk matters more to me than saving time. 
#For a quick, one-time question on a small file, I would still use Excel or Tableau, since setting up a full model isn't worth it for one answer.
